  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A line is a common tangent to the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;and the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. If the two points of contact <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> are distinct and lie in the first quadrant, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to ___ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let coordinate of point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>equation of tangent at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0074_9d69389ff63a.png\" style=\"width: 273px; height: 220px;\" /></p><p>centre of circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now Perpendicular distance =&nbsp;radius</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>So point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>(Since it lies in first quadrant)</p><p>For point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> which is foot of perpendicular from&nbsp;centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> to the tangent <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p>"
  }
}